WEBVTT

1
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.300
Right, bye. Bye, bye. Bye, we'll talk on Viber.

2
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.350
Come on, be good. Drive on, mate.

3
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.450
Oh, Beba, what are you doing here?

4
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.550
I live here.

5
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.950
Oh my God, I live here too, but I don't scare people at the front door.

6
00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.210
How was your day?

7
00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.360
How was your day, Ruža?

8
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:24.410
Oh, I went for a little walk, met some people, we chatted, hung out, so, nothing much.

9
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.300
The usual.

10
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:30.670
The usual? I warmed your slippers.

11
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.470
Thanks.

12
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.950
And your day?

13
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.020
My day?

14
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.320
My day was very interesting.

15
00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:44.200
You won't believe it, today I was kidnapped by Swiss flight attendants, taken to Israel, tortured there,

16
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:51.020
but when they found out you're my mother, they decided not to bomb the Balkan peninsula.

17
00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.370
So your day was really interesting.

18
00:02:54.420 --> 00:03:00.070
Ruža, who came in a garbage truck in front of the building a while ago?

19
00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.150
No idea.

20
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:10.200
Didn't we agree: when you don't know where you are, when you get lost, you get in a taxi, give the address and come here.

21
00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.230
Well, Beba, I did give the address.

22
00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:13.710
To whom?

23
00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.470
To Tarzan.

24
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.520
From the jungle?

25
00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:22.370
Oh, don't say that, don't. He's a very nice young man, ecologically aware.

26
00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.020
A garbage man?

27
00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.930
No, they're not garbage men, no.

28
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.400
No, they are city sanitation workers.

29
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:32.690
And when I was little, you told me: if you don't become somebody, you'll be a garbage man.

30
00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.570
Well, now you don't have to admit you haven't got very far.

31
00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.120
Where were you?

32
00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:44.960
Good grief, what's wrong with you, I wasn't on Mars.

33
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:52.470
And look, the tea is brewed, dear, I was in Ugrinovci.

34
00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:13.270
Where were you?

35
00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.850
I told you, I popped over to Ugrinovci.

36
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:21.890
You "popped" thirty kilometres, Ivana Španović would envy you.

37
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:23.270
How?

38
00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.820
Well, transport was organised, you know.

39
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.630
But I left a bit earlier, went out onto the motorway and hitchhiked.

40
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:36.080
I see all around me Hungarian plates, my God, maybe I'm heading to Hungary.

41
00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:42.490
So I cross the motorway to the other side and a gentleman in an Audi stops and picks me up.

42
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.570
Oh, how he drives, two hundred and fifty an hour, madness.

43
00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:58.850
And I see a sanitation truck coming this way, and I nicely, I didn't want to wait for a taxi, climb up, hang on to the truck and so I get here.

44
00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.980
And what if you had fallen off the truck, Ruža?

45
00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:06.790
Who, me fall? What's wrong with you, child? I spent my whole youth hanging on to trams.

46
00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.170
And what were you doing in Ugrinovci all day?

47
00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:19.070
Oh, it was very nice, you know, they gave me a sandwich, let me sit, and we all applauded. It was a lovely show, yes.

48
00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.340
You were an extra on a TV show?

49
00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:21.890
Yes, yes.

50
00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:23.830
Why didn't you call?

51
00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.940
How would I call you, they called me, me.

52
00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:27.300
Who did?

53
00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.570
Well, now I don't know exactly who. But it was through Facebook.

54
00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.250
You were messaging on Facebook again.

55
00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:37.160
I told you Facebook is full of paedophiles.

56
00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:41.170
What's wrong with you, Beba, I always message people on Facebook.

57
00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.650
Do you know how many likes I got on my profile picture? You have no idea.

58
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.870
But listen, I remembered.

59
00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:51.830
I put up my picture there from when I was thirty.

60
00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.230
Listen to me now.

61
00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.950
No more messaging on Facebook, I'll delete your profile.

62
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.610
You won't hang on to trucks, I'll ban your outings, do you hear,

63
00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.930
and you won't do this to me again.

64
00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:11.550
And if you keep behaving like this, we won't play Ludo for a month.

65
00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.550
Beba!

66
00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.250
Hello?

67
00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:31.030
Yes, city sanitation?

68
00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.060
Sorry, just a moment, please.

69
00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:40.690
Hello, sorry, Mr Tarzan, she won't come to that show of yours any more because she can't.

70
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.190
Tarzan, wait a moment now.

71
00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.370
Hello, Facebook, who is it from Facebook?

72
00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.790
Tarzan, wait.

73
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:54.270
Please, don't call my mother for TV shows any more, if it's needed, I'll come myself.

74
00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:01.830
Hello, Tarzan, listen, man, don't touch my mother, I'll pull out all your vines.

75
00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:20.710
Here you go.

76
00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:21.880
My fee.

77
00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:27.810
Go to the hardware shop. Buy a chain and tie me to the radiator,

78
00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.730
so that I can't go anywhere.

79
00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.710
Mum, sorry. Sorry I shouted.

80
00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.840
You don't know how lonely I am

81
00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:45.290
all day long here in this flat.

82
00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:52.560
Dear me, Beba, I'm making you breakfast.

83
00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:58.480
Just be careful not to set the building on fire, Mum.

84
00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:02.310
I'm in a hurry, I'm off to work.

85
00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:09.820
Please stay here, don't go anywhere.

86
00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:21.970
There, I'm begging you, don't hang on to trucks and don't hang out with Tarzan.

87
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:22.770
Okay?

88
00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.790
And what if we need milk?

89
00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.730
We have plenty of milk, don't worry.

90
00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:28.800
Well, okay, if I get bored.

91
00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.940
Then wait for me, I'll come.

92
00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.870
We'll play Ludo.

93
00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:00.620
And please, whatever you do, don't shake him.

94
00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:02.720
That's very important, sit down.

95
00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:05.240
Good afternoon, please, come in.

96
00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.770
Today we have a selfie-with-patients promotion.

97
00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:12.210
Yes, smile, man, one, two, three.

98
00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.430
What are you doing here, get out!

99
00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.470
Okay, and where would you start from?

100
00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.480
I'd like to see the doctor.

101
00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.760
Mhm, do you have an appointment?

102
00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.990
No, I'm his brother.

103
00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.690
No, I'm not the doctor, I'm his brother.

104
00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:40.380
Okay, now you've said you're his brother.

105
00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.640
I'll find him myself. Miša!

106
00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:46.770
Wait, please...

107
00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:48.990
Miša! Miša! Miša!

108
00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.800
You don't pay taxes.

109
00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:27.880
That's not true.

110
00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:30.940
I listen to Beethoven. I invest in culture.

111
00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:32.830
My tax obligations

112
00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.990
I leave to my accountant.

113
00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:43.840
Multi-talented, works with patients at reception,

114
00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:49.260
I even paid for a fantastic three-day accounting course for her.

115
00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.890
Oh, please, what you're saying is mobbing, sexism,

116
00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.910
typical male denial of gender equality.

117
00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:04.620
Doctor, is the check-up in fifteen days?

118
00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:05.650
Beauty.

119
00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:11.270
Do you know what kind of kitten you're going to be to me?

120
00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:16.560
Set up a meeting with check-in with my assistant,

121
00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:21.380
and we'll do the check-up in a by-the-way.

122
00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:22.410
Bye, bye.

123
00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:43.600
I know you're a failed student and a taxi driver,

124
00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.430
but please, mind how you express yourself

125
00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:49.850
in front of my patients in my medical facility.

126
00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:51.600
I came to talk about Mum.

127
00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:52.290
Mum isn't well.

128
00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.250
Well, okay, not well, not well, not well.

129
00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:55.170
And which of us is well?

130
00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:58.670
Beba, I'm a serious man.

131
00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:00.600
I have my job, my family

132
00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.070
and I'm a taxpayer.

133
00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:05.750
Look, I'm a serious man, but I can't take care of Mum alone.

134
00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.990
I don't know how serious a man you are,

135
00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:11.330
but I hear you still ask Mum to tell you bedtime stories.

136
00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:15.070
I hear you still want to play Ludo with her before bed.

137
00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:25.650
She's my mother, I call her every day, I ask her every day:

138
00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.000
Mum, how are you? Mum, are you okay?

139
00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:32.040
Mum, what do you need? We're constantly on the phone,

140
00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:34.930
but I don't call so that she'll tuck me in before bed.

141
00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.810
I don't like being tucked in either at forty,

142
00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.120
but I do it and put up with it, just so she feels alive.

143
00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.670
That's why I patch up noses, eyelids, ears, from head to toe,

144
00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.370
so people can see there's life in them.

145
00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.570
Come on, lie down here and let's see what your brother the surgeon can do for you.

146
00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:48.370
Come on, lie down here.

147
00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:49.530
I came here because of Mum.

148
00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.010
Come on, lie down so I can look at you, lie down here.

149
00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.160
Relax, don't be afraid, I'm your brother.

150
00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:03.430
Are you going to draw my blood?

151
00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.580
No, I won't draw your blood, now I'll melt your cracklings off.

152
00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:11.610
This, look, we'll cut all of this out like this.

153
00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.100
This here I'd tighten up a bit.

154
00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:20.400
I'll pump Botox in here.

155
00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.620
Here too we'll put a bit of Botox.

156
00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:23.650
Look, a moustache.

157
00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:27.060
I'll do permanent hair removal on that moustache.

158
00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.100
Dad had a moustache.

159
00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:35.700
What problems do you have, brother?

160
00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.310
I'll make you fifteen years younger.

161
00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.740
You'll look fifteen years younger.

162
00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:41.960
How long would that take?

163
00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.840
It will take forty-five minutes.

164
00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:46.620
Then could you give Mum some attention in that sense?

165
00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:47.640
She would be happy.

166
00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:50.120
I can't, Mum refuses the procedure.

167
00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:52.460
But she intervenes in my life.

168
00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:55.700
I dropped out of both faculties because of her.

169
00:14:55.750 --> 00:15:00.790
Well, okay, look, two academics in one family would be too much.

170
00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.340
I'm joking, just joking a bit, to see how you'd react.

171
00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.290
How can I help?

172
00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:08.910
With money.

173
00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.350
What do you think about silicone abs?

174
00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.720
Listen, it's a total hit in the world now.

175
00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:27.400
I'll implant silicone abs for you, but like this, in twelve parallel fields,

176
00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.380
but they look completely natural.

177
00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:29.710
I'm going.

178
00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:30.030
Why?

179
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:32.980
Because our mother has probably crossed the state border.

180
00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.800
Let's hope not, come on, hurry.

181
00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:36.530
Wait, please.

182
00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:41.980
Check at reception how much this preliminary examination costs.

183
00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:43.530
Please, sorry.

184
00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.440
Brother, brother, I have to, because of taxes.

185
00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:47.980
Okay, friend.

186
00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:40.570
Can I go home now?

187
00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.710
Madam, take it easy.

188
00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:49.140
How can I take it easy — you can take it easy, but I have a lot to do.

189
00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.100
Cooperate and you'll go home.

190
00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:55.820
Madam, do you know where you are?

191
00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:02.970
Madam, I'm not asking you philosophically, I'm asking you as a police officer: where are you?

192
00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:06.970
Well, probably, I mean, certainly, at the police.

193
00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:07.520
Clear.

194
00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:10.960
But do you know why you're at the police?

195
00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:18.150
I assume for political reasons.

196
00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.530
Yes. Drink some water.

197
00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.180
Read the report.

198
00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:32.720
In a children's toy shop you stole two boxes of Ludo.

199
00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:34.930
Do you like Ludo?

200
00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.630
How could I not adore it?

201
00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:37.050
Me too.

202
00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.920
Value: 1084 dinars.

203
00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:41.640
And? What happened then? Come on, come on.

204
00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:50.030
I went to buy Ludo, but my son Beba took all the money out of my wallet

205
00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:52.100
so that I wouldn't get robbed.

206
00:17:53.030 --> 00:18:01.290
So then you robbed that same shop, since the shop assistant says you put two boxes of Ludo in your bag.

207
00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:05.840
Oh no, madam, she probably put those boxes in her bag by accident.

208
00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.470
Oh no, yes, I put them in my bag,

209
00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.160
but because I wanted to go home to bring money.

210
00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:18.200
The shop owner called and reported the theft. Now you'll see.

211
00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:21.020
Well, I'll sue him, you know?

212
00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:23.540
Why would you sue him?

213
00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:30.440
What do you mean why? Because one box was missing four yellow pieces.

214
00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:33.580
Yes. And the price was criminal.

215
00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:37.690
Can we talk to your son?

216
00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:41.130
Oh, no. That will be very hard, you know.

217
00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.660
He's difficult. He won't let me go out.

218
00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:48.830
Okay, we don't have to talk.

219
00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:54.290
But I have another son, an older one, he's much more serious.

220
00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:59.740
He's a doctor, professor, surgeon, a famous plastic surgeon, Miša.

221
00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:01.580
Give me his number too.

222
00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:04.130
Well, he's very busy, but...

223
00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:05.100
Okay, here.

224
00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:09.150
Fantastic materials have arrived for me from Brazil.

225
00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.720
I mean, they haven't arrived yet, they're at customs.

226
00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.090
Once we get through all those customs rules,

227
00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:16.940
we can premiere them on you.

228
00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:21.350
And what if we enlarge them a bit?

229
00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:27.700
You'll look like a pendant on your own chest.

230
00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:31.750
How witty, doctor.

231
00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:32.560
Pardon?

232
00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:36.200
Nothing, I'm saying, you're witty.

233
00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.340
Pick up.

234
00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:39.090
Hello?

235
00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:43.540
Good afternoon, Popović's practice.

236
00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:51.260
The doctor is currently busy with a serious procedure.

237
00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:55.270
Well, I mean, sir, no...

238
00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:01.060
Yes, please.

239
00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:07.780
Doctor Popović, Miša, go ahead.

240
00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:16.010
Yes? Yes, yes, yes, Ruža is my mother, yes.

241
00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:21.650
What? Arrested at the police?

242
00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.790
For heaven's sake, why are you calling me?

243
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:29.840
Call Beba, Beba is in charge of her, why are you bothering me?

244
00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:31.430
But I have nothing to do with it, hello?

245
00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.690
You've reached Miša Popović, doctor.

246
00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:40.870
It always all falls on me.

247
00:20:57.660 --> 00:21:03.170
Oh, Miša, thank God, son, that you came.

248
00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:08.860
How did you manage to come after such a workload?

249
00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:14.810
Forget work, it's not important when it comes to you,

250
00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:17.720
money doesn't matter to me.

251
00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:21.690
Morality and honour come first.

252
00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:23.800
What is this about?

253
00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:24.260
About theft.

254
00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:27.070
How come? That's not characteristic of our family.

255
00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:29.890
Your mother was caught stealing in a shop.

256
00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.190
Mum, another name for morality is honesty.

257
00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:40.910
If you said her son did it, I might believe you.

258
00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:43.590
I mean her other son. Of course, I don't mean myself.

259
00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.290
For that there is prison or a fine.

260
00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:47.660
And what did Mum steal?

261
00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:53.010
Two packs of Ludo, one of which was slightly damaged at the bottom right,

262
00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:57.190
and everything was written in red letters in Serbian and Slovenian.

263
00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:07.110
Yes, yes, it said: Človek, ne jezi se.

264
00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:13.600
Oh come on, okay, I'm sure we can somehow solve this.

265
00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:15.760
And how, for example?

266
00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:18.340
Well, for example, we're human beings.

267
00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:18.960
Yes, and?

268
00:22:19.010 --> 00:22:21.640
In a civilised, creative way...

269
00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:22.670
Creative?

270
00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:25.020
You're some kind of artist here, huh?

271
00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.410
Oh, yes, indeed!

272
00:22:26.460 --> 00:22:28.670
He's a cosmetic surgeon, yes.

273
00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:39.990
Young lady, come here.

274
00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:41.910
Young lady?

275
00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:49.780
Have you perhaps thought about breast enlargement?

276
00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:57.370
Ruža!

277
00:22:57.420 --> 00:23:04.960
Ruža!

278
00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:11.950
Hello, Beba. Beba, where are you? Here, I've just got home.

279
00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:18.220
How did you get home when I'm at home and you're not?

280
00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:23.670
Kr, kr. Can you hear how it crackles? I can barely hear you.

281
00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:29.470
Ruža, come home at once! What are you doing, woman?

282
00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:31.600
Well, you said at once.

283
00:23:34.130 --> 00:23:34.940
Where were you?

284
00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:40.580
Well, look, Beba, it all started with our quarrel, but I wasn't long at the police.

285
00:23:40.630 --> 00:23:41.220
The police?

286
00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:42.860
They didn't put handcuffs on me.

287
00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:48.600
Well, I cooperated nicely, confessed everything and...

288
00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:50.810
What did you confess, Ruža?

289
00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:51.720
Well, the theft.

290
00:23:51.770 --> 00:23:52.720
You steal?

291
00:23:55.710 --> 00:24:06.530
You told me that tonight when you get back we'd play Ludo and then...

292
00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:08.120
Blow! Breathe out.

293
00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:09.450
You smoked.

294
00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:12.100
I didn't. They didn't let me.

295
00:24:13.070 --> 00:24:18.830
And then I looked for Ludo around the house and couldn't find it.

296
00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.740
And then I went to the shop to buy it.

297
00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:24.650
And there I took Ludo.

298
00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:30.140
Then at the last moment I saw that I had forgotten my money at home.

299
00:24:30.370 --> 00:24:33.850
So why didn't you call me?

300
00:24:33.900 --> 00:24:40.900
I didn't want to make you angry, so I called Miša.

301
00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:48.300
Where are you, Ruža, sweet sister?

302
00:24:48.350 --> 00:24:49.330
Oh, Tarzan.

303
00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:53.940
Listen, Ruža, that son of yours, is he a doctor?

304
00:24:53.990 --> 00:24:54.250
Yes.

305
00:24:55.260 --> 00:25:01.280
Good afternoon, doctor. Listen, my wife has a temperature.

306
00:25:01.330 --> 00:25:08.140
That's not important now, just help me bring the temperature down.

307
00:25:08.190 --> 00:25:12.190
I'm not a doctor, my brother is a doctor.

308
00:25:25.460 --> 00:25:26.320
My brother is a doctor,

309
00:25:26.370 --> 00:25:28.390
he's a plastic surgeon, he's for operations,

310
00:25:28.440 --> 00:25:29.490
you know, not for colds.

311
00:25:33.620 --> 00:25:35.870
Tarzan, just go, don't worry,

312
00:25:35.920 --> 00:25:38.390
I'll find out everything and let you know.

313
00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:40.830
We're friends, so don't worry.

314
00:26:06.260 --> 00:26:09.920
Ruža, what did you tell this poor man?

315
00:26:09.970 --> 00:26:13.370
And where is Miša? And why didn't he come with you?

316
00:26:13.420 --> 00:26:16.990
Oh, I completely forgot. Listen,

317
00:26:17.040 --> 00:26:21.470
Miša stayed there at the police. They detained him, you know?

318
00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:27.770
Yes? Well yes, wait, here, this note says he insulted an official

319
00:26:27.820 --> 00:26:30.960
and offered a bribe to another official.

320
00:26:31.010 --> 00:26:37.430
You have to go there, vouch for him and pay some fine, you know?

321
00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:38.430
Come on, run.

322
00:26:38.900 --> 00:26:43.800
How can I run when we have to play Ludo?

323
00:26:43.850 --> 00:26:44.740
Oh, well yes.

324
00:26:44.790 --> 00:26:46.540
Come on, let's play.

325
00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:47.390
The third time.

326
00:27:02.210 --> 00:27:06.680
Look, I have three pieces in the home, you don't have a single one.

327
00:27:12.330 --> 00:27:13.670
Why don't they arrest you?

328
00:27:13.720 --> 00:27:16.280
Well, Dad kept asking himself that too.
